[00:09.04]These days, we use credit cards more and more and they all look almost identical.
[00:15.72]But money is still with us, in coins and banknotes.
[00:21.04]The designs are different and all over the world we can see examples of really interesting and beautiful banknotes.
[00:30.22]The designs usually celebrate the country – its history, its geography, its animals and birds.
[00:38.61]Here are some examples of banknotes from different parts of the world.
[00:45.20]Mexico
[00:46.12]In Mexico the currency is the peso.
[00:50.00]The smallest banknote is 20 pesos, and the biggest is 1,000 pesos.
[00:57.24]One side always has the face of a famous person from Mexican history and the other side has well-known places in the country.
[01:07.40]On the $500 note there is a portrait of the famous Mexican artist Frida Kahlo.
[01:17.34]Europe
[01:18.60]Many countries in Europe use the euro, but the banknotes are exactly the same for each country.
[01:26.02]On one side, there is a picture of a gate, window or entrance, and on the other side, a bridge.
[01:34.22]The pictures represent different kinds of architecture from all over Europe.
[01:42.56]Turkey
[01:43.62]In Turkey the currency is the Turkish lira, and there are six different banknotes.
[01:50.78]Each one shows Kemal Atatürk, the founder of the Turkish republic, on the front side, and another famous figure from Turkish history on the other side.
[02:05.00]Brazil
[02:06.00]The currency in Brazil is the real (plural, reais).
[02:12.60]The notes are in different colours, but they all have a picture of the Effigy of the Republic (a national symbol of Brazil) on one side, and various animals, birds and fish on the other side.
[02:26.66]One of the most beautiful is perhaps the R$50 note, which has a picture of a jaguar.
